# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
screenshot.png
screenshot.request
fx*.png
# Ctrl+P debug region captures (see src/region_capture.rs). Ephemeral; the folder's CLAUDE.md is kept.
debug_screenshots/*.png
# The note box written beside each capture. Ignored with its PNG, for the same reason: the pair is
# machine-written per capture. A finding worth keeping gets rewritten as a dated, titled note next to
# them — those are committed, and this pattern is narrow enough not to catch one.
debug_screenshots/region_*.md
# Spatial FPS probe output (src/perf_probe.rs) — machine-written every run, pure measurement.
debug_screenshots/fps_trace.csv
debug_screenshots/fps_hotspots.md

# Offline behaviour-search outputs (see src/squad_ai/coevolve.rs). Regenerated by `train prior` /
# `train evolve`; nothing in the shipped game reads them. The prior is a frozen reference the search
# reproduces from the authored brains, and the elite archives churn every run — committing either would
# version stale, machine-generated data. A *blessed* archive, once one is adopted into the game, gets a
# distinct committed name.
assets/config/baseline_prior.ron
# Every `elites_*.ron` is a machine-generated search output (squad/swarm/world/levels/audio/behavior/policy
# co-evolution + neuroevolution + POET). None are read by the shipped game; a *blessed* archive adopted into
# the game gets a distinct committed name.
assets/config/elites_*.ron

# `cargo train` island-model output: per-island archives + logs from a parallel search fan-out. Same
# rationale as elites_*.ron — machine-generated; the winner is applied via `train apply`, never committed here.
islands_out/

# Snapshots of every archive that was ever baked (`train apply` keeps one per bake so an old elite stays
# reviewable after the next run overwrites `elites_*.ron`). Machine-generated and potentially large, same as
# the archives they copy — but note the *ledger* that indexes them, BAKES.md, IS tracked: it is the review
# trail for a moved golden, and a review trail nobody else can see is not one.
assets/config/bake_history/

# Claude Code per-project state (worktrees from other sessions, transcripts) — never commit.
# `.claude/settings.json` is the exception and IS tracked: it carries the PreToolUse hook that denies
# `screencapture` / `macinput.py` / `vinput.py`, and a policy only this machine enforces is not a
# project policy. Per-developer overrides belong in `.claude/settings.local.json`, still ignored.
# Written as `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded — the negation below is silently dead if the directory itself is ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# omp per-project session state (plans, transcripts, artifacts) — never commit. Same rationale as
# `.claude/*` above: this is one machine's conversation with an agent, not project content.
.omp/

# Per-developer Cargo overrides (e.g. a machine-specific build.target-dir for local build isolation).
# MUST NOT be committed: a hardcoded absolute path broke CI on ubuntu-latest for every commit
# ("failed to create directory /Users/…: Permission denied"). Each machine keeps its own local copy.
.cargo/config.toml

# Evidence written by `visual_capture::title_screen_matches_golden` when it fails — for one
# review, never committed. The golden beside it IS committed.
tests/golden/*.actual.png

# Blender/python leaves these beside the conversion scripts.
scripts/__pycache__/

# **Maps moved to assets/emerge/maps/ on 2026-08-16 and are TRACKED there.** They used to be written
# beside the kit that drew them; a map now resolves against every bound kit merged, so there is no
# kit to be beside. This rule is one level deep and does not match `maps/`, which is why the
# subdirectory was chosen: a stray scratch map dropped at the project root stays ignored, and an
# authored map in `maps/` is content.
assets/emerge/*.map.ron
# ...with one deliberate exception, kept for the same reason it was written. `break_room` is a
# REGRESSION FIXTURE rather than a scratch map: without a committed map, a schema change could break
# every authored map with nothing failing.
!assets/emerge/break_room.map.ron

# The VLM labeler's endpoint config — carries the API key, never committed.
.env

# Runtime session state from `bevy-debugger-mcp`, which writes relative to the working
# directory — so running it from the repo root drops this here. Not source.
debug_sessions/

# **Derived assets are build output.** `assets/derived.json` is the recipe and the hashes; the bytes
# live in a content-addressed cache on the asset library share. `cargo fvs assets sync` fetches them,
# `... build` regenerates them from source with Blender. Committing them is committing build
# artifacts — `assets/scp610/scp-610.glb` is in this repo's history three times, at 27, 5 and 4 MB.
# See scripts/derived_assets.py.
assets/ozea_kit/*.glb

# macOS Finder metadata. Never useful, and it lands in a commit the moment anyone runs
# `git add -A` in a directory Finder has opened.
.DS_Store

# **The built demo site is build output, and it is 358 MB of it.** `web/index.html`, `web/play.html`
# and `web/style.css` are the source and are committed; `web/dist` is ten Bevy wasm modules at ~36 MB
# each, regenerated by `scripts/build_web.sh` and published by CI's `site`/`pages` jobs from an
# artifact. Committing it would put a third of a gigabyte of binary into the pack forever, which is
# the same mistake `assets/scp610/scp-610.glb` is in this history three times for.
web/dist/

# Inter-agent scratch channel — never committed.
agents_chat.md
